{
 "id": "lem-per-smooth-local-dimension",
 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Local topological dimension formula for smooth morphisms",
 "statement": "Let $g:P\\to Q$ be a smooth morphism [def-sbc-smooth-morphisms] between locally Noetherian schemes [pqf-def-locnoeth]. For any $p\\in P$, set $q=g(p)$ and let $P_q=P\\times_Q\\operatorname{Spec}\\kappa(q)$ be the scheme-theoretic fibre [def-pc-scheme-fibre], with its point corresponding to $p$. With local topological dimensions as in [def-kun-topological-dimension-at-point],\n$$ \\dim_p P=\\dim_q Q+\\dim_p P_q.$$\nHere local topological dimension is the infimum of the dimensions of open neighbourhoods, not the dimension of the local ring. In particular, when $g$ is smooth of constant relative dimension $d\\geq0$, the last summand is $d$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/stacks-project/morphisms.tex",
  "place": "Tag 0AFF, lemma-smoothness-dimension"
 },
